window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>The multi-species crew of the <i>Veracity</i> are enjoying some well-deserved R&amp;R after informing the galaxy about the spread of the time-bending Messiah drug. Now that the galaxy has been saved again, the crew begin to see each other in a new light. </p><p>Unfortunately, in the <i>Veracity</i>'s wake lie a string of crimes - and someone has got to pay. Former assassin Raena Zacari is hauled back to the weapons-free pleasure planet Kai to answer charges of kidnapping, murder, and the theft of an Imperial-era diplomatic transport: the <i>Veracity</i> itself. </p><p>In the meantime, something is moving in the undersea city Raena destroyed on the Thallian homeworld. Has the worst mass-murderer the galaxy has ever known been cloned back from the dead? Can the <i>Veracity</i>'s crew lay the ghosts to rest without Raena's lethal skills? </p><p><i>No More Heroes</i> mixes courtroom science fiction with sweeping space opera that features aliens, androids, drug dealers, journalists, and free-running media hackers. Following <i>The Dangerous Type</i> and <i>Kill By Numbers</i>, <i>No More Heroes</i> is the final book in Loren Rhoads's epic trilogy. </p>"; 
